  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n4 4 8\n6 4 3\n6 3 0\nOutput:\n4 4 4\n4 4 4\n4 4 4\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n6 8 9\n1 8 1\n9 4 9\nOutput:\n9 9 9\n9 9 9\n9 9 9\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n4 6 9\n6 4 1\n8 8 6\nOutput:\n6 6 6\n6 6 6\n6 6 6\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n8 8 6\n4 6 9\n8 3 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform the input grid by filling every cell with the most frequent value\n    (the mode) appearing in the original grid.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    grid : list[list[int]]\n        A rectangular grid of integers.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list[list[int]]\n        A grid of the same dimensions where all cells contain the mode value.\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import Counter\n\n    # Flatten the grid to count occurrences of each value\n    flat = [cell for row in grid for cell in row]\n\n    # Find the mode(s)\n    freq = Counter(flat)\n    max_count = max(freq.values())\n    # In case of a tie, choose the smallest value (consistent deterministic behavior)\n    mode = min(val for val, cnt in freq.items() if cnt == max_count)\n\n    # Reconstruct the output grid with the same shape, filled with the mode\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows else 0\n    result = [[mode] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    return result",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform the input grid by filling every cell with the most frequent value\n    (the mode) appearing in the original grid.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    grid : list[list[int]]\n        A rectangular grid of integers.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list[list[int]]\n        A grid of the same dimensions where all cells contain the mode value.\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import Counter\n\n    # Flatten the grid to count occurrences of each value\n    flat = [cell for row in grid for cell in row]\n\n    # Find the mode(s)\n    freq = Counter(flat)\n    max_count = max(freq.values())\n    # In case of a tie, choose the smallest value (consistent deterministic behavior)\n    mode = min(val for val, cnt in freq.items() if cnt == max_count)\n\n    # Reconstruct the output grid with the same shape, filled with the mode\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows else 0\n    result = [[mode] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    return result",
